  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "Q1 (the direction). A routed approver holds decision rights but not record read. Which model does v18 adopt? Measured facts every option must answer: the gap has three classes (A no CRUD read → 403; B OWD private → 404; C app RLS → 404); the #7345 case is C; a share cures B only and cannot pass CRUD, RLS or the organization wall.",
      "options": [
        "A — route-time explicit record-share grant (maintainer pre-recorded preference). Business need: cures class B only (measured 200 after grant); A and C stay 403/404 (grant refused SHARING_NOT_ENABLED; RLS AND-composed); the motivating #7345 case (C) is not fixed; corpus has 0 approval targets on private-OWD objects; production demand NOT MEASURED. Long-term: explicit, auditable (sys_audit_log row measured), listable by the owner, inside the wall (non-member share stays 404); but needs a new ShareSource member in packages/spec (spec seat), its own revoke/sweep semantics, grant/revoke companions at 10 slate-write sites plus position-holder changes with no shared transaction, a boot backfill for in-flight pending requests, and cannot bind position/email/team literal slots at route time. AI-safety: partial guarantee (private-OWD only) is invisible to an author unless refused at publish on non-enforcing targets; otherwise 'declared approver ⇒ can read' holds for one class of three. Startup: new capability, zero measured pull, three lanes (services, identity, spec).",
